As others have said, the only thing ESSENTIAL to win the game is the
amulet of Yendor and staying alive. However, to give it a shot, I try
to always have the following items:

Easy to get: (Means you never need to wish for it)
 Pick-axe
 unicorn horn
 mirror

Harder to get, but may be found:
 Good weapon (+8 enchantment, preferably Frost Brand, Stormbringer or
  Excalibur, rustproof)
 Good armour (AC < -15, preferably. A magic marker and blank
  scrolls...)

What I don't do without (although it's perfectly possible to finish
the game without it, I NEVER try to. Experience speaks...):
 Ring of conflict (whithout question the best item in the game)
 Magic resistance

What I usually want to have (but may do without):
 Ring of levitation
 Ring of teleport control (or intrinsic tel cont)
 Speed boots
 Reflection (shield or amulet)
 Amulet of life saving
 All the needed intrinsics (fire, cold, sleep, poison)

So: when I get that WoW here's my normal wishlist:
(everything blessed unless otherwise stated)
(and - of course - I don't wish for it if I have already found it!)
2 scrolls of charging
magic marker
ring of conflict
3 scrolls of genocide (R, L, N and then I don't genocide anything else)
GDSM (or wand of polymorph if I have good armour and magic resistance)
shield of reflection (don't wish for it if I have an amulet of
  reflection) 
speed boots (but I have usually already found a pair by then)
amulet of life saving

If I have a wand of polymorph I try to make DSM of the four dragons in
the castle before wishing anything, so I know what I need to wish for.
If I get intrinsic disintegration resistance I don't wish for the
shield, but rather something else.
